    ["“壁炉在夏日是否会熄灭呢？然而它们是明亮的……\""] = "“Will the fireplace go out in summer? Yet they are bright……”",
    ["　　占卜可以按获得“启示”的方式分为三类：\n　　第一类，借助询问人自身的“力量”，通过“感应”获得启示，比如塔罗占卜和扑克占卜。\n　　第二类，由占卜人主导，通过对自然界或询问人提供的信息进行计算和推测来获得启示，如灵数、占星。\n　　第三类，向第三者寻求答案，常见的是“魔镜占卜”。这种占卜方式实在太有趣了！通常是向七位正神祈求答案，如果我向其他存在祈求会怎么样？\n\n备注：\n　　今天格拉西斯先生说这里曾有一位真正的占卜家，那位只是看了他一眼，就知道他肺部有问题，这又是什么原理？真希望有机会见见那位莫雷蒂先生。"] = "Divination can be divided into three categories based on how \"revelations\" are obtained: \n The first category is to obtain revelations through \"sensing\" by using the \"power\" of the person asking, such as Tarot divination and poker divination. \n The second category is led by the diviner, obtaining revelations through calculation and speculation based on information provided by nature or the person asking, such as numerology and astrology. \n The third category is seeking answers from a third party, the most common being \"Magic Mirror Divination.\" This method of divination is really interesting! Usually, one prays to the seven orthodox gods for answers. What would happen if I prayed to other existences? \n \n Note: \n Today, Mr. Glacis said that there was once a real Seer here. That person only took one look at him and knew he had lung problems. What is the principle behind this? I really hope to have the chance to meet that Mr. Moretti.",
